      },
      "message": "fix(app): face, trace and contour on imported meshes with float-noise corners\n\nThe #241 part (cutouts.camproj) is a closed mesh whose shared corners\nscatter by up to 1.04 um and whose top stands 3e-13 mm uneven. Three\nreal failures on main, each a wrong refusal:\n\n- slicer: chord ends welded by a rounded 1 um key split pairs that\n  straddled a rounding boundary, so the closed part sliced \"open\"\n  (12 dangling chord ends). Ends now weld within 2 um through a\n  neighbourhood search (new geometry::slice_weld); a 0.1 mm gap still\n  refuses as open.\n- silhouette fallback: the facet-shadow union used Region::new's nesting\n  parity, so bottom facets nested under top facets became phantom holes\n  (27 on this part, up to 433 mm2) - a chain-only Face pick was clipped\n  by them and refused on gaps that were not there. It is now a pure\n  union (Region::union_all).\n- section at Top of Part: a plane at the highest noisy corner met only\n  that corner and read \"no material\". The section retries 1 um lower\n  on an empty answer as it already did on an error; a plane that truly\n  misses names the Z span to move Top of Part Z into.\n\nThe face-pick Facing \"15.15 mm gap\" refusal was #260, fixed by PR #313\n(1da9695b). Box selection is filed as #979.\n\nPinned by an_open_mesh_rim_pick_faces_the_whole_top_with_no_phantom_holes,\nsub_micrometre_corner_scatter_still_welds_into_a_closed_slice,\na_tenth_of_a_millimetre_gap_is_still_open,\na_whole_model_contour_at_a_noisy_top_sections_the_part and\na_top_plane_above_the_part_still_refuses_and_names_the_span.\n\nFixes #241\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
